# Front (src/)

## Layers

- `domain/` — pure presentation rules (`attention.ts`: labels logic, filters, usage formatting),
  `copy.ts` (typed access to **all** UI text; the text is in `locales/`), `generated/` (ts-rs types from `crates/application/src/view.rs`
  — never edit; regenerate with `cargo test -p awr-application`).
- `application/` — `WarRoomStore` (framework-free; components subscribe with `useWarRoom(store)`)
  and `ports.ts` (WarRoomGateway, TerminalGateway, IntegrationGateway, FilterStorage).
- `infrastructure/` — `tauriGateway.ts` (commands/events), `demoGateway.ts` (a fake room used in a
  plain browser, for design and screenshots), `localFilterStorage.ts`.
- `ui/` — components; `pixel/` for the War Room canvas.
- `main.tsx` is the composition root: Tauri adapters inside the app (`__TAURI_INTERNALS__`), demo ones
  otherwise.

## Rules

- Components never inline user-visible text: `copy.<area>.<key>` (functions for parametrised text),
  backed by `locales/*.json` (`i18n.mdc`). Status labels arrive already translated from Rust; the demo
  builds its `STATUS` from the same catalog (`coreStatus`) — `extraActivity` compares text.
- Several agents: `providerName`/`copy.providerShort`, `launchableAgents`, `mixesAgents` (cards show
  an agent tag in its colour, `data-provider` → `--agent`, only when the room mixes them). One header
  button, `AgentsMenu`, lists every integration (dot per agent: connected, incomplete, off, not
  installed) with connect/reinstall/disconnect and the login toggle; banners only for found agents not
  yet connected. "+ Agent" becomes a menu when more than one agent can be started. Unpriced usage
  shows tokens only (`usageLabel`).
- Filters start folded to one line (remembered in localStorage); the header must fit on two lines at
  1500 px with the preview open.
- New data from the core: add it in `view.rs`, regenerate, then fixtures (`src/test/fixtures.ts`) and
  the demo (`demoGateway.ts`) — the demo is what screenshots show.
- Styling: one `ui/styles.css` on tokens. `--c` = attention color via `data-attention`; `--k` = skill
  source color via `data-source`; amber `#f59e0b` = stalled. No CSS framework, no inline colors.
- Links in agent Markdown never navigate the app window (`Markdown.tsx` → `openExternal`, http(s) only).
- The detail panel is the one place for a session's depth: task, last reply, usage, changes (on
  demand), skills, subagents (clickable → subagent view, Esc goes back), timeline, diff overlay. "Read
  the answer" (header and the reply's section, also for a subagent's result) opens `AnswerReader`: the
  Markdown at reading size over the whole window (portal), with copy; its Esc is caught first.

## Trigger table

| If you… | Read |
|---|---|
| touch the pixel-art War Room (layout, drawing, font, drones) | `frontend-pixel-art.md` |
| need to see the result | skill `verify` (screenshots) or subagent `awr-screenshotter` |
